<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arnoldo Alemán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1946</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arnoldo Alemán is a Nicaraguan Liberal politician who was mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/managua">Managua</a> and then president of Nicaragua from 1997 to 2002. His power-sharing pact with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniel-ortega">Daniel Ortega</a>'s Sandinistas divided state institutions between their two parties and lowered the threshold for winning the presidency. He was convicted of embezzlement and money laundering in 2003, a verdict later overturned by the Supreme Court in 2009.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arnoldo-aleman.jpg" alt="Arnoldo Alemán" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arnoldo Alemán · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ArnoldoAleman1997.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
